      "card_ids": ["C03", "C20", "C24"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Azosemide, the closest structural analog with the same chloro-sulfamoyl anthranilate core and heteroarylmethylamino side chain, has an L1 absolute oral bioavailability of 20.4% in fasted healthy humans, meeting the F >= 20% threshold; the L2 urinary-recovery estimate of 10% is indirect and does not overturn the L1 gold value.",
      "card_ids": ["C04", "C26"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Cirrhosis-condition contexts consistently show high oral bioavailability: metoclopramide 79 to 82% and tolfenamic acid about 100%, with L2 values of 113 to 126%.",
      "card_ids": ["C06", "C12", "C13", "C22", "C30", "C16", "C25", "C29"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L4 intestinal absorption, solubility, and permeability records concern unrelated molecules such as sulfasalazine, diclofenac, Ac-5-ASA, and other compounds; they provide no query-specific absorption evidence and do not change the prediction.",
